<div class="bg-primary text-white text-center p-5 rounded-3 shadow-sm mb-4 mt-5 position-relative" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0d6efd 0%, #0a58ca 100%);">
    <h3 class="fw-bold mb-2">Enterprise Security Compliance Integrity Gateway</h3>
    <p class="mx-auto col-lg-8 text-white-50 mb-4">Click below to read through the strict database privacy data masking and cryptographic validation policies governing all asset storage accounts.</p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-light fw-bold text-primary px-4 py-2 text-uppercase shadow-sm" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#privacyPolicyModal">
        <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-lock-fill"></i> Read Privacy Policy Ledger
    </button>
</div>

<div class="modal fade" id="privacyPolicyModal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header bg-dark text-white">
                <h5 class="modal-title fw-bold" id="exampleModalLabel"><i class="bi bi-shield-shaded text-info"></i> ShieldOps Governance & Privacy Directive</h5>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close btn-close-white" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body p-4 text-start">
                <h6 class="fw-bold text-primary border-bottom pb-2">1. Data Allocation Enclaves</h6>
                <p class="small text-muted" style="text-align: justify;">
                    All profile credentials, addresses, and transaction hashes recorded inside the ShieldOps SQL Server instance undergo encryption validation layers. System logs trace user allocations solely to execute session-level shopping state manifests.
                </p>
                <h6 class="fw-bold text-primary border-bottom pb-2 pt-2">2. Cryptographic Session Lifetime Protection</h6>
                <p class="small text-muted" style="text-align: justify;">
                    Session values map via strict HTTP-only configuration wrappers inside the local host container environment middleware. Memory caches systematically isolate user vectors, forcing cart drops automatically upon expiration or sign-out execution cycles.
                </p>
                <h6 class="fw-bold text-primary border-bottom pb-2 pt-2">3. Return Policy Matrix & Asset Audits</h6>
                <p class="small text-muted" style="text-align: justify;">
                    Logistical assets qualify for reverse pipeline allocation returns within a maximum lifecycle limit of exactly 7 days. Beyond this temporal framework, automated database tracking validation gates drop approval requests instantly to maintain stock accounting integrity.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer bg-light">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close Manifest</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>